tags: pasta, salmon, seafood, dinner, lemon, quick
---

Cook the @rigatoni/pasta{16%oz} according to package directions.

Meanwhile, season @salmon fillet{1%lb} with @salt and @pepper to taste and bake at 350 degrees F for ~{15-20%minutes}, depending on thickness.

Once the pasta is cooked, drain and toss with @garlic{1%clove}(minced), @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp}, @basil leaves{1/2%cup}(finely chopped) and season with salt and pepper to taste.

Add @lemon juice{2%tbsp}, @lemon zest{1%lemon}(of one lemon) and @capers{2%tsp} to the pasta and toss to mix.

Flake the salmon into bite-size pieces.

Gently toss salmon with the pasta.

Dish and serve hot topped with freshly grated or shaved @Parmesan cheese{}.